    "episode_id": "VR-488814",
    "evidence": "The September 2026 bank reconciliation for Hollis Facilities Management (account ending 4402) does not show equal adjusted balances. Adjusted bank balance: 18,642.35 + 2,150.00 deposit in transit - 480.00 (cheque 1043) - 1,215.40 (cheque 1047) - 96.25 (cheque 1049) = 19,000.70. Adjusted book balance: 19,290.70 - 40.00 bank charges not yet entered = 19,250.70. The two adjusted balances therefore differ by 250.00 (19,000.70 vs 19,250.70), so the claim that they are equal is false. The statement 'No other reconciling items were identified' and the preparer's note 'Reconciled, no differences' do not close the gap: they assert a conclusion the arithmetic contradicts, and the unreconciled 250.00 is exactly the kind of item that would have been listed had it been identified. To make the sides agree the book side would need an adjusted figure of 19,000.70 (a cash book balance of 19,040.70) or the bank side an extra +250.00, and neither appears. Uncertainty: this reconciliation schedule is the only evidence in the case, so the individual figures are taken as printed; the discrepancy is a matter of the printed arithmetic rather than of missing documents.",
